    <string name="interest_rating_guide_title">Interest rating guide</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_intro">These guidelines reuse the Descente-Canyon criteria to make ratings more consistent.</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_4_label">4/4</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_4_title">This canyon is truly fantastic: it is among the most beautiful routes that exist.</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_4_description">It is complete: a long and original route, with continuous interest and no dull section. It combines aquatic and playful aspects (swimming, jumps, slides...) with technical aspects (rappels, handlines...). The setting is grandiose (landscapes, narrow gorges, erosion shapes...).</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_3_label">3/4</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_3_title">It has the same qualities as above, but they are less sustained.</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_3_description">Something small is missing for it to reach the top category: it may be a little too short, or it may have exceptional sections without continuity... It remains a very beautiful route.</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_2_label">2/4</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_2_title">This canyon has one of the previous qualities, but is not complete.</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_2_description">For example, a very beautiful narrow gorge, but short or too dry. Beautiful erosion features, but little verticality... Or genuinely beautiful sections spoiled by serious pollution (rubbish, water quality...).</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_1_label">1/4</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_1_title">This is a canyon of interest mainly for enthusiasts.</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_1_description">For example, it has a short, very beautiful section, but with a prohibitive approach. Or the &quot;canyon&quot; character is weak (very small waterfalls, no real gorge...). In short, it feels like it could be enjoyable, but something is always missing.</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_0_label">0/4</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_0_title">Either it is no longer really a canyon, or many factors make the route completely uninteresting.</string>
    <string name="interest_rating_guide_0_description">No waterfalls, no gorge, a short canyon full of logs and unstable blocks, with a long boar-track approach through thorny bushes... In short, avoid it completely.</string>
